<div id="InPageEditor" style="height: 100%;"><textarea id="editor{{editorIndex}}Src">Loading...</textarea></div>

<div class="wmd-docs" style="max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
<h2>WYSIWYG Markdown Editor</h2>
<p>Edits Markdown visually and saves plain Markdown files. It runs inside <code>StandaloneEditor</code> with the flavour <code>WYSIWYGMarkDown</code>, in the same way as the Simple HTML and Markdown editors. Open any file with <code>?pageName=/Some/Page&amp;fileName=notes.md</code>.</p>

<h3>Views</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Visual</b>: edit with the toolbar and shortcuts, no Markdown needed.</li>
<li><b>Source</b>: edit the Markdown directly in the Markdown editor (CodeMirror).</li>
<li><b>Split</b>: source and visual side by side, kept in step as you type in either one. On narrow screens they stack.</li>
</ul>
<p>A file that is opened and saved without visual edits is saved exactly as it was written. Visual edits regenerate the Markdown in a standard layout (see below). If a file contains something visual editing would change, a warning says so when it opens and again on the first visual edit. Use Source to edit such files safely.</p>

<h3>Supported Markdown</h3>
<p>CommonMark plus GitHub-style tables and strikethrough, rendered with markdown-it and written back with turndown (see /OpenForum/Javascript/MarkDown).</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Feature</th><th>Written as</th></tr>
<tr><td>Headings 1 to 4</td><td><code># Heading</code> to <code>#### Heading</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Bold, italic, strikethrough, inline code</td><td><code>**bold**</code>, <code>*italic*</code>, <code>&#126;&#126;struck&#126;&#126;</code>, <code>`code`</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Lists, nested lists</td><td><code>- item</code>, <code>1. item</code>, nested items indented to match</td></tr>
<tr><td>Links and images</td><td><code>&#91;text&#93;(url)</code>, <code>!&#91;alt text&#93;(url)</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Quotes and rules</td><td><code>&gt; quote</code>, <code>---</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Code blocks</td><td>Fenced with three backticks and an optional language</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tables</td><td>GitHub tables with a header row; a line break inside a cell is kept as <code>&lt;br&gt;</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>HTML comments</td><td>Kept as they are</td></tr>
<tr><td>kbd, sup, sub, u, mark, ins, abbr, details, summary, iframe, video, audio</td><td>Kept as HTML, since Markdown has no syntax for them</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Not supported in the visual view: footnotes (they become plain text), and other raw HTML, which is simplified to its Markdown equivalent. Images that are uploaded or pasted are stored inside the file as data URLs.</p>
<p>Pasting from Word, Google Docs or web pages converts the content to Markdown. Colours, fonts and layout are removed, and a note says so. Pasting into a code block always pastes plain text.</p>

<h3>Keyboard shortcuts</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Keys</th><th>Action</th></tr>
<tr><td>Ctrl+B, Ctrl+I, Ctrl+Shift+X, Ctrl+E</td><td>Bold, italic, strikethrough, inline code</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ctrl+Alt+1 to 4</td><td>Heading level 1 to 4 (press again to remove)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ctrl+Shift+8, Ctrl+Shift+7, Ctrl+Shift+9</td><td>Bullet list, numbered list, quote</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ctrl+K</td><td>Insert or edit a link</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z</td><td>Undo, redo</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tab, Shift+Tab</td><td>Next or previous table cell (Tab in the last cell adds a row)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ctrl+Enter</td><td>Start a new paragraph after a code block, table or quote</td></tr>
<tr><td>Arrow keys, Home, End</td><td>Move along the toolbar when it has focus; Escape returns to the text</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Embedding in your own app</h3>
<p>Embed the editor with <code>StandaloneEditor</code>, as the Journal does with the Simple HTML editor. A working example with its own interface, autosave and a word count is at <a href="/OpenForum/Editor/Editors/WYSIWYGMarkDownEditor/Example">/OpenForum/Editor/Editors/WYSIWYGMarkDownEditor/Example</a>.</p>
<pre><code>OpenForum.includeScript("/OpenForum/Editor/Editors/StandaloneEditor.js");

var myEditor = new StandaloneEditor({
  flavour: "WYSIWYGMarkDown",
  elementId: "MyEditorHost",
  editingPageName: "/MyApp/Notes",
  editingFileName: "notes.md",
  editorPage: "/MyApp/",
  ui: "/MyApp/my-editor-ui.html.fragment",
  autoSave: true,
  canSetPageTitle: false
});</code></pre>
<table>
<tr><th>Option</th><th>Use</th></tr>
<tr><td>flavour</td><td><code>WYSIWYGMarkDown</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>elementId</td><td>The element the editor is placed in.</td></tr>
<tr><td>editingPageName, editingFileName</td><td>The file to edit.</td></tr>
<tr><td>editorPage</td><td><b>Always set this to your own page.</b> Without it, StandaloneEditor reopens the last file edited with this flavour on any page in the browser, ignoring editingPageName and editingFileName, and autosave then writes to that file.</td></tr>
<tr><td>ui</td><td>Your own page fragment instead of the standard File, Desktop and Actions bar. It must contain an element with <code>id="editor&amp;editorId;"</code>. Copy the <code>confirmRetrieveModal</code> from the example too: without it, unsaved changes kept in the browser can't be offered back after a crash or reload. In the fragment, <code>&amp;editor;</code> is replaced with the editor object, for example for a Save button.</td></tr>
<tr><td>autoSave</td><td>Saves every 10 seconds while there are changes. This is one page-wide setting shared by every StandaloneEditor on the page.</td></tr>
<tr><td>canSetPageTitle</td><td>Set to false so the browser tab title isn't changed.</td></tr>
<tr><td>editorsPage</td><td>Only for testing a Development copy of the editor: where editor scripts are loaded from.</td></tr>
</table>
<ul>
<li>Wait until <code>myEditor.getCodeMirror() != null</code> before using the editor.</li>
<li>To react to edits, wrap <code>myEditor.storeChanges</code> and call the original from your version. Don't replace it: the original keeps the browser copy used for recovery.</li>
<li><code>myEditor.getValue()</code> and <code>myEditor.setValue(markdown)</code> read and write Markdown. <code>myEditor.save()</code> saves.</li>
<li><code>myEditor.getEditor().setMode("visual")</code>, <code>"source"</code> or <code>"split"</code> changes the view; <code>getMode()</code> reads it.</li>
<li>Several editors can be used on one page.</li>
</ul>
</div>

